#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0342 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "ANRLOC (the guard AND key column) is not declared -- data that WOULD fire if ANRLOC existed and were constant. empty(ANRLOC) over an absent column folds to a broadcast TRUE, not makes it a broadcast FALSE and the AND short-circuits, so the rule EXECUTES and reports nothing -- even though the operator, left alone, would have dropped the absent key, regrouped on [PARAMCD] and flagged row 3. Pins 'the key-side guard suppresses the drop-and-regroup'. Verdict is noViolation WITH execution, not skipped."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col ANRLO   type=Num
---
S1 | 001 | GLUC | 5.0 | 3
S1 | 002 | GLUC | 5.1 | 3
S1 | 003 | GLUC | 5.2 | 4
